WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.465
FedRAMP emphasizes continuous monitoring rather than one-time assessment.

00:00:03.465 --> 00:00:07.251
Cloud environments change, vulnerabilities appear, configurations evolve, users change,

00:00:07.251 --> 00:00:11.037
incidents occur, and services continue to develop after authorization.

00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:14.823
Continuous monitoring helps organizations maintain visibility into security controls,

00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:19.030
vulnerabilities, system changes, operational risks, and remediation activities over time.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.815
Monitoring may include vulnerability scanning, configuration management, incident reporting,

00:00:22.815 --> 00:00:26.601
plan of action updates, control status reporting, change tracking,

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:28.705
and review of security-relevant events.

00:00:28.705 --> 00:00:33.332
The goal is not to collect information for its own sake.

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:35.435
Monitoring should help agencies, providers,

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:41.745
and stakeholders understand whether the cloud service continues to operate within an acceptable risk posture.

00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:43.848
Continuous monitoring also supports accountability.

00:00:43.848 --> 00:00:47.213
If a control weakens, a vulnerability remains open,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:52.682
or a system change affects the security boundary, decision makers need current information.

00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:56.889
For technical teams, continuous monitoring connects FedRAMP to daily operations.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:01:00.254
Patch management, logging, alerting, change control, vulnerability remediation,

00:01:00.254 --> 00:01:04.881
incident response, and configuration review all contribute to the security picture.

00:01:04.881 --> 00:01:08.246
The practical takeaway is that FedRAMP is ongoing.

00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:11.611
Authorization is not the end of the work;

00:01:11.611 --> 00:01:17.080
it is part of a lifecycle that depends on sustained visibility and management.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.445
Continuous monitoring also supports better conversations with agencies.

00:01:20.445 --> 00:01:22.969
Current information about vulnerabilities, changes, incidents,

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:29.700
and remediation gives stakeholders a clearer view of whether the service remains within expected risk boundaries.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.748
For program teams, this means monitoring evidence should be reliable and repeatable.

00:01:34.748 --> 00:01:39.795
The organization needs processes that can produce current information without rebuilding the

00:01:39.795 --> 00:01:42.740
entire security story from scratch each month.
